--- !u!114 &431040390
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 431040385}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e1bdf894aea541e4ca7c2a34c3db6452, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OrganDescription
  textUI: {fileID: 1044996059}
  audioSource: {fileID: 2000439513}
  teksID:
  - "Trakea / Batang Tenggorokan: \nSaluran udara utama berbentuk tabung yang menghubungkan
    laring (pangkal tenggorokan) ke bronkus. Trakea dilapisi cincin tulang rawan
    agar tetap terbuka."
  - "Bronkus & Bronkiolus: \nCabang dari trakea yang masuk ke paru-paru (Bronkus).
    Saluran ini bercabang lagi menjadi lebih kecil seperti pohon (Bronkiolus) untuk
    menyebarkan udara ke seluruh bagian paru-paru."
  - 'Alveolus:

    Kantung udara mikroskopis di ujung bronkiolus. Di sinilah terjadi
    pertukaran gas kritis: oksigen masuk ke dalam darah, dan karbon dioksida dikeluarkan
    dari darah.'
  audioID:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1e4c6c893e4a9354e9138b45fd67da03, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8fb990005e6c0c74b85610af8a7bc531, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: ab987ef3dfc8f6942b7cf594baed602e, type: 3}
  teksEN:
  - 'Trachea:

    The main tube-shaped airway connecting the larynx (voice box)
    to the bronchi. The trachea is lined with cartilage rings to keep it open.'
  - 'Bronchi & Bronchioles:

    Branches of the trachea that enter the lungs (Bronchi).
    These tubes branch further into smaller, tree-like structures (Bronchioles) to
    distribute air to all parts of the lungs.'
  - 'Alveoli:

    Microscopic air sacs at the ends of the bronchioles. This is where
    critical gas exchange occurs: oxygen enters the blood, and carbon dioxide is
    removed from the blood.'
  audioEN:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3a3f5523f78628f43bd314746ba8bf4b, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7038527707c1024499e4360b1ba7440b, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3574952ca78927b4ca007a0ee97abf25, type: 3}
  teksFR:
  - "Trach\xE9e:\nLa principale voie respiratoire en forme de tube reliant le larynx
    aux bronches. La trach\xE9e est tapiss\xE9e d'anneaux de cartilage pour la maintenir
    ouverte."
  - "Bronches et Bronchioles: \nBranches de la trach\xE9e qui p\xE9n\xE8trent dans
    les poumons (Bronches). Ces conduits se ramifient encore en structures plus petites
    semblables \xE0 un arbre (Bronchioles) pour distribuer l'air dans toutes les
    parties des poumons."
  - "Alv\xE9oles:\nSacs alv\xE9olaires microscopiques \xE0 l'extr\xE9mit\xE9 des
    bronchioles. C'est l\xE0 que se produit l'\xE9change gazeux critique : l'oxyg\xE8ne
    entre dans le sang et le dioxyde de carbone en est extrait."
  audioFR:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3d77d47066f931e4b8596382950a9c61, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9254299b217e4bd4c939bcdfb5241dfd, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7850a39ef06de854c9431e6d3b28ce62, type: 3}
