--- !u!114 &1770074222
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1770074217}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e1bdf894aea541e4ca7c2a34c3db6452, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OrganDescription
  textUI: {fileID: 1044996059}
  audioSource: {fileID: 2000439513}
  teksID:
  - "Otak Besar / Cerebrum: \nBagian terbesar dari otak. Mengendalikan fungsi tingkat
    tinggi seperti pikiran sadar, emosi, memori, pembelajaran, serta memproses informasi
    dari panca indera."
  - "Otak Kecil / Cerebellum: \nTerletak di bagian belakang bawah otak. Berfungsi
    mengatur keseimbangan tubuh, postur, dan mengoordinasikan gerakan otot agar halus
    dan akurat."
  - "Batang Otak / Brainstem: \nMenghubungkan otak dengan sumsum tulang belakang.
    Mengendalikan fungsi otomatis tubuh yang vital untuk bertahan hidup, seperti
    detak jantung, pernapasan, dan tekanan darah."
  audioID:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: f9c7f749b49b95e48bb5eee08d0fc023, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: af94f82fa64b7e84ebd7864d371dd123, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: af521b2938ffce446aa1ae6c08fa6fcf, type: 3}
  teksEN:
  - "Cerebrum: \nThe largest part of the brain. It controls higher-level functions
    such as conscious thought, emotions, memory, learning, and processes information
    from the senses."
  - "Cerebellum: \nLocated at the lower back of the brain. It functions to regulate
    body balance, posture, and coordinate muscle movements so they are smooth and
    accurate."
  - "Brainstem: \nConnects the brain to the spinal cord. It controls automatic body
    functions that are vital for survival, such as heart rate, breathing, and blood
    pressure."
  audioEN:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1524dc36a04fcf44980a3d81347a142b, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8d93686644dc61b4287abf897dcec859, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: c7c0a6ca666c2fc4b9ab79d8cdfbb666, type: 3}
  teksFR:
  - "Cerveau / Cerebrum: \nLa plus grande partie du cerveau. Il contr\xF4le les fonctions
    de haut niveau telles que la pens\xE9e consciente, les \xE9motions, la m\xE9moire,
    l'apprentissage et traite les informations provenant des sens."
  - "Cervelet / Cerebellum: \nSitu\xE9 \xE0 l'arri\xE8re et en bas du cerveau. Sa
    fonction est de r\xE9guler l'\xE9quilibre du corps, la posture et de coordonner
    les mouvements musculaires afin qu'ils soient fluides et pr\xE9cis."
  - "Tronc c\xE9r\xE9bral: \nRelie le cerveau \xE0 la moelle \xE9pini\xE8re. Il contr\xF4le
    les fonctions corporelles automatiques vitales pour la survie, telles que le
    rythme cardiaque, la respiration et la pression art\xE9rielle."
  audioFR:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: f856a69d81f1d034d84a6866b2b2f85d, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: b1be07b36b843e04e97cc41be563c136, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6cbbfc6bf6886f34792cb8f50387b97f, type: 3}
