--- !u!114 &1782657468
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1782657463}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e1bdf894aea541e4ca7c2a34c3db6452, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OrganDescription
  textUI: {fileID: 1044996059}
  audioSource: {fileID: 2000439513}
  teksID:
  - 'Serambi / Atrium:

    Serambi (Atrium) kanan dan kiri terletak di bagian atas
    jantung. Fungsinya menerima darah kotor dari tubuh dan darah bersih dari paru-paru
    sebelum dipompa ke bilik.'
  - "Bilik / Ventrikel: \nBilik (Ventrikel) terletak di bagian bawah dan memiliki
    otot yang lebih tebal. Bilik kanan memompa darah ke paru-paru, sedangkan bilik
    kiri memompa darah ke seluruh tubuh."
  - "Katup Jantung / Valves: \nKatup jantung berfungsi seperti pintu satu arah. Katup
    memastikan darah mengalir ke arah yang benar dan mencegah darah mengalir balik
    ke ruang sebelumnya."
  audioID:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: d2b13376f11011b49a1243a7cc2d3db5, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: c6e56039e9546644f9bb008dc6d2125c, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0ffc12c9eb7bee442885bf37a5789e4d, type: 3}
  teksEN:
  - "Atrium: \nThe right and left atria are located at the top of the heart. Their
    function is to receive deoxygenated blood from the body and oxygenated blood
    from the lungs before pumping it to the ventricles."
  - "Ventricles: \nThe ventricles are located at the bottom and have thicker muscles.
    The right ventricle pumps blood to the lungs, while the left ventricle pumps
    blood to the rest of the body.\n"
  - "Valves: \nHeart valves act like one-way doors. They ensure blood flows in the
    correct direction and prevent it from flowing back into the previous chamber."
  audioEN:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: ef3f7c441d74ba244a24cb11416ae9b0, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: c21437080cf7be34b9715a7eb6364233, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8c08cb89655db2a419dc82a933152512, type: 3}
  teksFR:
  - "Oreillettes / Atriums: \nLes oreillettes droite et gauche sont situ\xE9es dans
    la partie sup\xE9rieure du c\u0153ur. Leur fonction est de recevoir le sang d\xE9soxyg\xE9n\xE9
    du corps et le sang oxyg\xE9n\xE9 des poumons avant de le pomper vers les ventricules."
  - "Ventricules: \nLes ventricules sont situ\xE9s dans la partie inf\xE9rieure et
    poss\xE8dent des muscles plus \xE9pais. Le ventricule droit pompe le sang vers
    les poumons, tandis que le ventricule gauche pompe le sang vers le reste du corps."
  - "Valves cardiaques: \nLes valves cardiaques fonctionnent comme des portes \xE0
    sens unique. Elles assurent que le sang circule dans la bonne direction et l'emp\xEAchent
    de refluer vers la cavit\xE9 pr\xE9c\xE9dente."
  audioFR:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7101e458f7950b74aa2cf2dbdb9f9cd8, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 63d41892557134e4fa38b12cfe7de5bf, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6abb42f52976e4043a049b76a7da03b1, type: 3}
